---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const pageTitle = "Free Tech Pack Template Guide for Fashion Brands | SDF";
const pageDescription = "Complete tech pack template guide. What every garment tech pack needs | flat sketches, measurements, BOM, construction details. Free template included.";
const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": pageTitle,
    "description": pageDescription,
    "author": { "@id": "https://sdfltd.com/#org" },
    "publisher": { "@id": "https://sdfltd.com/#org" },
    "url": "https://sdfltd.com/insights/tech-pack-template-guide/",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://sdfltd.com/insights/tech-pack-template-guide/"
  }
];

---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} schema={schema}>

  <div class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;">

    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <p style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: #FFFFFF; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">
        <a href="/" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;"> | </span>
        <a href="/insights/index" style="color: #aaa; text-decoration: none;">Insights</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;"> | </span>
        <span style="color: #FFFFFF;">Tech Pack Template Guide</span>
      </p>
    </nav>

    <article>

      <header style="max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.25em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Production Guide</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 200; color: #fff; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: 0.01em;">
          Tech Pack Template Guide | What Every Garment Tech Pack Must Include
        </h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #aaa; line-height: 1.9; margin: 0;">
          A tech pack is your blueprint for production. It tells the manufacturer exactly what to make. A complete tech pack prevents errors, reduces sampling rounds, and ensures your vision becomes reality.
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">What Is a Tech Pack?</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">A tech pack is a document that contains all specifications for a garment. It includes flat sketches, measurements, materials, construction details, and care instructions. Manufacturers use tech packs to produce your design accurately.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Without a tech pack, manufacturers must guess your requirements. This leads to errors, delays, and extra sampling costs. A good tech pack is clear, detailed, and unambiguous.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">SDF Clothing requires a tech pack for all custom orders. We provide a free template to help you create professional tech packs.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Flat Sketches</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Flat sketches show the garment from front and back views. They are technical drawings, not fashion illustrations. Include front view, back view, and any special details like pockets or zippers.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Sketches should be clean and proportional. Use consistent line weights. Show all seams, stitches, and construction details. Color is optional but helpful for multi-color designs.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Include detail callouts for complex areas. Zoom in on collars, cuffs, plackets, and other intricate features. This helps manufacturers understand construction.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Measurements</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Measurements specify the size and fit of the garment. Include a measurement chart for all sizes. Specify points of measure clearly. Common points include chest, length, sleeve, waist, and inseam.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Include tolerance for each measurement. Standard tolerance is plus or minus 1 centimeter. This allows for normal production variation while maintaining quality standards.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Specify grade rules. Grade rules define how measurements change between sizes. Standard grade rules vary by garment type and target market.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Bill of Materials</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">The bill of materials lists all components of the garment. Include main fabric, lining fabric, interlining, thread, buttons, zippers, labels, tags, and any other trims.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">For each material, specify composition, weight, color, and supplier if known. Include consumption estimates. This helps manufacturers calculate costs accurately.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Specify material alternatives. If your primary fabric is unavailable, what alternatives are acceptable? This prevents production delays.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Construction Details</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Construction details explain how the garment is assembled. Specify stitch types, seam allowances, and construction methods. Include notes on special techniques like embroidery or printing.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Specify seam finish. Common finishes include overlock, serging, and flat-felled. Specify hem finish. Common hems include blind hem, double-fold hem, and coverstitch.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Include construction callouts on sketches. Show seam directions, stitch placements, and special construction areas.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Fabric and Trim Specifications</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Specify fabric composition, weight, and finish. For knit fabrics, specify GSM. For woven fabrics, specify thread count. Include color standards using Pantone or color swatches.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Specify trim details. Button size, zipper length, label dimensions. Include placement instructions for all trims. Specify thread color and type.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Include performance requirements. If fabric needs specific properties like water resistance or stretch, specify these clearly.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Care Instructions</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Care instructions tell consumers how to wash and care for the garment. Include washing method, drying method, ironing temperature, and any special care requirements.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Use standard care symbols. These are recognized internationally. Include text instructions as backup. Specify if dry cleaning is required.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Care instructions affect fabric selection. Choose fabrics that can withstand the care method your customers will use.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Packaging Specifications</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Specify packaging requirements. Include polybag type, folding method, and labeling. Specify how many garments per polybag and per carton.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Include shipping label requirements. Specify barcode placement, country of origin labeling, and any retail packaging requirements.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Packaging affects cost and presentation. Balance protection needs with environmental considerations and retail requirements.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Common Tech Pack Mistakes</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Incomplete information is the most common mistake. Missing measurements, unclear specifications, or vague descriptions cause errors. Be specific and detailed.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Inconsistent units cause confusion. Use metric or imperial consistently. Do not mix centimeters and inches in the same document.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Ambiguous language leads to misinterpretation. Avoid words like "approximately" or "similar to." Use precise measurements and clear descriptions.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Free Template Structure</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">A good tech pack template organizes information logically. Start with basic information like style name, season, and target market. Follow with sketches and measurements.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Include materials and construction details in the middle. End with care instructions and packaging specifications. This flow follows the production process.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">SDF Clothing provides a free tech pack template. Our template includes all essential sections and follows industry best practices.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Tech Pack FAQ</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>Do I need a tech pack for simple designs?</strong> Yes. Even simple designs need specifications. Without a tech pack, manufacturers cannot produce your design accurately.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>Can I use photos instead of sketches?</strong> Photos are helpful but not sufficient. Technical sketches are clearer for production. Use photos as reference, but provide professional sketches.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>What if I don't know technical details?</strong> Manufacturers can help fill in technical specifications. Provide your design vision and let them suggest construction methods.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>How detailed should measurements be?</strong> Include all critical measurements. More detail is better. Specify points of measure clearly to avoid confusion.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;"><strong>Can I update the tech pack during production?</strong> Updates during production cause delays and costs. Finalize your tech pack before production begins. Minor updates are possible but should be minimized.</p>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;"><strong>What format should I use?</strong> PDF is standard. Some manufacturers accept other formats. Check with your manufacturer for their preferred format.</p>

      <div style="text-align: center; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00; background: #050505; margin-top: 3rem;">
        <p style="color: #fff; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-weight: 300;">
          Need help creating your tech pack? SDF Clothing provides a free tech pack template and guidance on technical specifications. We help new brands create professional tech packs.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" style="display: inline-block; background: #e00; color: #fff; padding: 0.9rem 2.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; transition: background 0.2s;">
          Get Free Template ?
        </a>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #aaa; margin-top: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8;">
        For a complete overview of clothing manufacturers in Bangladesh | including tech pack requirements, production processes, and quality standards | read our <a href="/clothing-manufacturers" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">complete clothing manufacturers guide</a>.
      </p>

    </article>

  </div>

    
    </BaseLayout>




